Nethack (the 286 version) is overlayed, and 640k is not enough for the basic
movements, etc that you list.

Hmmm: 640K.  Data and tables use up ~300k.  Basic movement, attack, monster
movement, etc (I think) uses up ~500k.  Don't forget Dos (30k)  That's more an
a meg already.

The overlay units are loaded into memory on an 'on demand' basis and stay in
memory until there isn't enough space.  That's why getting 2 Meg allows for
the dramatic speed increase, and ~3 meg requires NO disk hits (except
switching levels and loading an overlay for the first time)

